permission-feeds-manage = Manage feeds
feed-unknown-kind = I do not know that kind of feed. Use youtube, reddit, twitch, x or pixiv.
feed-unsupported-kind = { $kind } feeds are not supported yet.
feed-handle-unsupported = A @handle is not supported yet. Give the channel link (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC...) or its UC... id.
feed-bad-target = That is not a YouTube channel id (UC...) or a link to a channel.
feed-full = This server already has the most feeds it may have.
feed-kind-full = This server already has the most feeds of this kind.
feed-exists = This feed already posts to that channel.
feed-channel-missing = That channel is not in this server.
feed-channel-denied = The bot cannot send messages in that channel.
feed-added = Feed added as { $id }. Its first look only records what is there; new items are posted after that.
feed-removed = Feed removed.
feed-not-found = No feed has that id.
feed-none = No feeds yet. Add one with /feed add.
feed-resumed = Feed resumed.
feed-tested = The newest item was posted as a test.
feed-busy = Too many feeds are being read right now. Try again in a moment.
feed-empty = That feed has no items yet.
feed-read-failed = The feed could not be read right now.
feed-more = { $count } more new items were not posted one by one.
feed-paused-channel-missing = paused: the channel is gone
feed-paused-channel-denied = paused: the bot may no longer post in the channel
feed-paused-failures = paused: the feed failed too many times in a row
